WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.610
Class 3-B?

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.760
Ms. Kuroi!

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:05.920
Yeah, yeah...

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.040
Yo!

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:33.960
Sis!

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.210
How'd the test go?

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:37.420
Same as always...

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.090
Another disaster.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.680
We have more free time during testing...

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.430
...but you end up following your usual schedule...

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.680
...so you have to cram the night before, right?

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:53.520
You should act more like someone applying for college...

00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:00.450
Thousands of manga and games were confiscated from the suspect's room.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.030
Based on his methods, it is believed that other crimes can be attributed to him.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.450
<i>Another story about this...</i>
Based on his methods, it is believed that other crimes can be attributed to him.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:04.950
<i>Incredible...</i>

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.200
There was another person like you on the news.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:12.290
Every time this happens, it makes me think how it isn't fair.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:15.460
They always use these kinds of manga as examples.

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.420
There are good manga out there.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.670
They just never get mentioned.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.380
R-Right...

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:24.970
I feel kinda bad.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:27.930
You're a good person!

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:33.060
Usually, people just make fun of me for being a desperate freak.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.940
Looking at the people I know...

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:40.030
...sisters tend to absorb
characteristics from one another.

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.570
Like you and Cousin Yui...

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.110
Or Kagami and Tsukasa...

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.120
I was talking about that with Big Sister this morning.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.000
<i>You're really close to Miyuki-chan.</i>

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.170
<i>You're as close as sisters.</i>

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:00.550
I see.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:01.840
It was absorption?

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:02.840
Kona-chan!

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:04.760
Happy birthday!

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:10.390
I would have forgotten if Tsukasa hadn't mentioned it.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.940
Congratulations.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.440
Thanks, everyone!

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:20.190
It makes me happy when people celebrate my birthday...

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:23.820
...but at this age, I really can't be happy about getting older.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.740
Nah.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.870
It makes me super happy.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.370
Why?

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:31.450
Do you want to get a driver's license?

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.750
Because I can play adult games now.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:38.200
Haven't you been openly playing them the whole time?

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.340
Of course not...

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.300
You've grown older...

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.340
...without aging mentally or physically.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:48.760
Let me go!

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.140
Miyuki probably gets mistaken for someone older.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.980
'Cause Yuki-chan looks like an adult.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:56.940
When I go out in my normal clothes...

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.230
...I occassionally get mistaken for an office lady.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.820
So they skip straight past college.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:04.610
In your case...

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.780
...if you walk around in normal clothes...

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.530
...they'll think you're in grade school.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.280
Say what you want.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:11.780
Starting today, I'm an adult!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:13.700
What are you talking about?

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:14.950
Besides...

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.540
...if you're an adult now...

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:19.380
...shouldn't you be less passionate about anime and manga?

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.050
Y-You still need to have a child-like
heart filled with passion and dreams!

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.880
Make up your mind...

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:29.930
This?

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.430
While Big Sister's at work...

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:37.000
...we're going to secretly prepare a birthday party for her.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.850
Sorry I'm late!

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.900
Okay!

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.520
Let's get everything ready.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.610
Yes!

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:06.210
And here's a call from Konata.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.630
Wonder if she'll be coming home soon.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.220
Konata?

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:10.930
Sorry!

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:12.350
Forgot to tell you...

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:15.180
...but my co-workers are throwing a party for me...

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.850
...so I won't be eating dinner at home.

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.730
And I'll be coming home late.

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.270
Yutaka.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.690
Doesn't this taste great?

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:26.360
We worked hard.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:26.980
Yui-chan.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:28.280
You can take that off now.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.280
Future aspirations, huh...

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:33.490
I have dreams and stuff...

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:35.970
...but it's kind of hard when you stop and think about it.

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.200
That's right.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.870
The major you decide on...

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:42.670
...will have an effect on your career.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.920
First is nutritional science.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.130
Second is fashion design.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.340
Third is marketing.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:54.050
Since I like cooking and sewing.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:56.930
So you wrote down your dreams.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:58.770
And what about you, Miyuki-san?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:01.810
I want to be a doctor...

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.560
...so while I didn't write down colleges...

00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:07.320
...I put medical schools for all three choices.

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.190
That's our Miyuki-san.

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.400
You have a clear goal.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.530
What about you, Kagami?

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:14.030
Me?

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:16.660
My first choice is law.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:18.450
My second choice is economics.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:19.910
My third choice is literature.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.160
Sheesh.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.830
Too boring.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.380
Is that a bad thing?

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:25.750
What about you?

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:28.840
Here we go.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:30.670
Some people try to turn it into a joke.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:31.470
Actually...

00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:34.140
...do you have any talents besides making faces?

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:35.260
Talents...

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:42.310
I can name every Poke**n!

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.310
Th-That's definitely amazing.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:46.440
But it has nothing to do with your future.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:49.520
Here it is!

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:54.530
I'll go pay for this.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.160
When you buy magazines and manga...

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.120
...you always take one from the bottom.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.000
Everybody's already touched the ones on top.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.170
I'd rather buy a clean one.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:07.880
I know what you mean.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:09.880
Like when I go to a sushi-go-round...

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:11.340
...I order straight from the chef...

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.900
...instead of taking them off the belt.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:14.600
You know...

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:17.090
Most of the ones on the belt are already dry.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:19.850
You do that?

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.600
What a bad customer.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.220
No way!

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:23.180
You don't?

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:24.350
What a scrooge.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.980
I've been wondering...

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:30.190
How can you stand reading books that are all text?

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:31.320
Don't you get sleepy?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.970
But this is a light novel.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.910
It basically feels like reading manga.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.580
Sure about that...

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:40.950
There are plenty of insert pictures...

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.870
...and the writing is simple.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:44.120
Why don't you give it a try?

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.170
W-Well, you know...

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.250
They already made an anime of it.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:48.830
So I'll just watch that.

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:49.920
If it were a manga...

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:52.710
...you'd be talking about how the original has its own merits...

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:54.760
...and check both out.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.340
Just read it already.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.800
I must respectfully pass.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.180
But you know...

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:02.560
You read lots of stuff besides light novels.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.890
How should I put it...

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:06.480
When I become more culturally refined...

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.770
...my soul becomes richer.

00:08:09.770 --> 00:08:11.610
Well, it's like food for the soul.

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:13.940
I see.

00:08:14.570 --> 00:08:15.220
What is it?

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:16.280
By that reasoning...

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.450
...the snacks are for making your body richer.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:21.490
Shut up!

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:24.500
Aren't there also light novels...

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.910
...serialized in the magazines you read?

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:28.290
Not just comics.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.540
I look at the pictures...

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.800
So despite everything you say...

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.840
...your love is pretty weak.

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:40.090
You skim, huh?

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:41.470
Fine!

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.140
Be that way.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:42.850
I'll read it!

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:44.810
Hey, it's okay.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:47.270
No need to push yourself.

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:51.060
I only skim 'cause I have lots of other stuff to read!

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.980
Fine by me.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.530
I didn't say a thing.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.190
Oops!

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.070
I forgot my world history textbook.

00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:02.780
I left it on my desk after studying.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:03.910
Konata.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.830
Lend me your world history textbook.

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:07.330
You didn't take it home, right?

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.300
Okay.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.500
Did you forget yours?

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:11.750
That's unusual.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:13.460
Here.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:16.840
Hiiragi.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:19.590
This is one fun textbook.

00:09:20.050 --> 00:09:21.720
No, this is...

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.120
Not getting anywhere...

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:32.350
Guess I'll find something to drink.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.150
Sheesh.

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.110
Huh?

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:40.570
Thought there was some leftover from last time...

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:43.390
Gives me a chance to get some fresh air.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:45.780
They're closed!

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:48.540
This is some kind of challenge, isn't it?

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:54.770
Your total comes to 320 yen.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:56.630
Huh?

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:03.720
What's wrong, Sis?

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:04.470
Yeah...

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.140
When you're in a bad mood...

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.430
...you make a bunch of little mistakes...

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:09.020
...which just makes your mood worse, right?

00:10:09.640 --> 00:10:10.640
I know what you mean!

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:13.310
You can't seem to do anything right.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:16.150
Like a negative spiral?

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.070
That's right!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.280
I baked a cake.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:20.860
Want some?

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:22.360
Yay!

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:24.160
Studying is rough...

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.780
...so you have to take breaks now and then.

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:27.540
That's it!

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.120
I'll bake cookies tomorrow!

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:32.040
That'll relieve stress.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.540
I'm counting on you!

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:38.380
Now I've got a new source of stress.

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.380
Right?

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.220
Don't you agree, Iwasaki-san?

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:43.550
That's right.

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:48.450
Those two are so busy that they keep missing each other.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.600
I know what you mean.

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:55.650
<i>That's right.</i>

00:10:55.650 --> 00:10:57.310
<i>Big Sister is applying for college...</i>

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:59.570
<i>...so I shouldn't disturb her studying!</i>

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.690
Sorry...

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:03.240
I'm going to talk softer.

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:06.620
Yu-chan.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.830
Let's play a game after you're off the phone.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:09.660
Get your game on!

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.000
Say what?!

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.460
Guess this is the last year I'll be wearing this uniform.

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.840
That gets me thinking...

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:24.010
There's something inside.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.140
My favourite handkerchief that I thought I had lost...

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.510
It was in my summer uniform's pocket, huh?

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.650
Didn't we have some wasabi octopus?

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:39.690
What is this?

00:11:43.070 --> 00:11:44.950
What was this?!

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.240
It's changed so much I can't tell...

00:11:47.990 --> 00:11:50.240
It sure rains a lot in the rainy season.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.160
Sure does.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.160
It starts getting really hot...

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.960
...and then we switch to our summer uniform just in time...

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:58.450
...but the temperature can suddenly drop which sucks.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:00.920
You guys are still here?

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:04.630
You're lucky since you can change your clothes whenever you want.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:07.300
What are you talking about?

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:11.640
It's so much easier when you don't have
to think about what to wear every morning.

00:12:11.640 --> 00:12:14.560
You're really wack, Teacher.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.400
Ya-ho!

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.310
It's the rainy season!

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:22.150
So humid!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.190
Cousin Yui.
Sis.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:26.150
It sucks how it's always raining.

00:12:26.150 --> 00:12:27.490
Do you want some tea?

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:29.200
Please.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:35.080
On a happier note...

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.670
...it's almost been a year since you got married, right?

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.330
That's right.

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:40.380
Time sure flies.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.340
The image of a raining sky...

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:48.340
Is like the image of Cousin Yui's heart when her husband
is away on business with their first anniversary coming up...

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:50.800
Her heart is...

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:53.310
Sorry...

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:54.890
That was my fault.

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.060
It's okay.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.230
I'm used to this kind of pain.

00:12:59.230 --> 00:12:59.940
Here.

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:02.300
Have something warm to drink.

00:13:05.230 --> 00:13:07.850
But I'm still depressed...

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:10.820
It's delicious.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.200
That's a relief.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:13.990
Sheesh.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.700
At this rate, my love's going to rust eventually!

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.040
If you took it to an auto repair place...

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:22.630
...it'd probably be good as new after 45 minutes.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:26.590
You could at least comfort me...

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.590
Sorry.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:29.530
Force of habit.

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:32.280
Hello?

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.560
So you can come home!

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.930
Didn't even take 45 minutes.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.270
It was like an instant.

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:41.100
That's right.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:46.190
You haven't gotten your clothes back from Matsuri?

00:13:46.190 --> 00:13:47.440
That's bad.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.990
If you don't ask for them back soon...

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:52.620
...she'll say they're hers.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:53.990
That would be bad!

00:13:53.990 --> 00:13:56.540
I really like those!

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.750
I envy Kagami-san and Tsukasa-san...

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:04.920
...for having two sisters.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:05.630
Pretty much.

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:07.000
Really?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.340
In my opinion...

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:11.930
...I'd rather be an only child like you two.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:13.240
Right?

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:16.640
I get that feeling sometimes...

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:18.180
But you know...

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:21.280
...you can do so much more with a bigger cast.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:23.190
Like the story set in olden America...

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.900
...of a mother and her four daughters...

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.940
...waiting for the father to return.

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:32.030
Or an enigmatic band of female thieves who target art.

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.160
One, two.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:37.370
Huh?

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:39.040
One too many.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:40.250
Seriously...

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:43.920
She turns every conversation into
something about anime or games.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:45.790
Hey, Kagami.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:48.300
Did you buy the stuff for dinner?

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.760
Did you forget to tell her, Tsukasa?

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.010
Sorry...

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.010
What? What?

00:14:54.010 --> 00:14:54.680
What's going on?

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:56.720
Geez. Did you forget?

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:59.310
Mom and Dad are out tonight.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:01.390
Their trip was today?

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:02.770
So then...

00:15:02.770 --> 00:15:05.310
...we were supposed to buy groceries for dinner.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:07.610
I completely forgot.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.860
I called Kagami's cell...

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:11.820
...and left a message.

00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:15.910
Matsuri.

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:18.450
Just use what's in the fridge.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:22.160
I finally get a chance to cook...

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:23.580
Just let it go this time.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:26.000
Sheesh.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:28.110
This is all your fault!

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:29.710
Sorry...

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:33.300
Fine.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:35.170
I'll go now.

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:39.010
Geez...

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:41.060
You just had to go and say that.

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.220
But...

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.600
And does she even know what to buy?

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:47.810
Geez, man...

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:50.110
She doesn't even like to cook that much.

00:15:50.110 --> 00:15:51.730
Why's she so worked up?

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:53.570
Sis!

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:57.740
Tsukasa.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:03.450
Sis...

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:05.540
You don't have the shopping list, right?

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:11.800
They're late...

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.800
If you're gonna worry...

00:16:13.800 --> 00:16:16.140
...you should have gone yourself.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.260
You're late.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:25.180
What's wrong?

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.890
Matsuri was really worried.

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:31.730
The usual store was out of saffron.

00:16:31.730 --> 00:16:34.900
I said that curry powder would work...

00:16:35.530 --> 00:16:40.740
...but Sis insisted that we find some so
we went to the supermarket farther away.

00:16:41.030 --> 00:16:41.870
Geez.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.120
You didn't have to do that.

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:45.330
So sorry.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.290
Come on.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:50.710
Let's make dinner.

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:52.460
Whew, I'm starving.

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:55.420
Here.

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:56.510
Sorry for the wait.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:59.130
That just leaves Matsuri's masterpiece.

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:00.500
I'm done!

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:04.510
It looks great!

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.480
Looks like it was cooked just right.

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:11.520
Hey, Matsuri.

00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:14.260
When did you learn how to cook this?

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:17.280
I went to this one restaurant with
some college friends a while back..

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.950
...and this was on the menu.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.410
It was so good...

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.620
...that I wanted to let you all try it...

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:24.370
...so I asked for the recipe.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:27.370
I'm surprised they gave it to you.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:29.570
Anyway, chow down.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:33.540
Huh?

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:34.920
What's wrong?

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:35.920
Listen to this.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.220
Your father got the date wrong.

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.340
What do you mean?

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.300
The reservation was apparently for next week.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.060
Straight out of a comedy...

00:17:47.100 --> 00:17:48.060
Dinner now?

00:17:48.060 --> 00:17:49.430
You haven't eaten?

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:51.980
Paella, is it?

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.690
Matsuri made it!

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:55.440
Oh.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:56.880
That's amazing!

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.780
But Kagami bought the ingredients for it.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:03.570
She went all the way to the farther supermarket.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:14.910
Then I'll help myself.

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.130
Good idea.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:19.130
This is pretty good.

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:21.930
Who took the mussel?

00:18:21.930 --> 00:18:23.050
Mussel?

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:24.590
Was I not supposed to?

00:18:24.590 --> 00:18:25.890
Unbelievable!

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:28.100
I was saving that for last!

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.810
Then write your name on it.

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:32.230
Geez. Stop fighting.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:34.480
Yo.

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:36.900
I'll hang out with you after school today.

00:18:36.900 --> 00:18:38.860
Do you need to buy something?

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:41.900
Shin** Yamada's new book.

00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:44.240
Though we have a bunch of homework lately...

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:46.120
...so I don't really have time to read.

00:18:47.030 --> 00:18:50.540
I also have a pile of unread manga by my pillow.

00:18:51.710 --> 00:18:55.000
But I end up going for a new one.

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.840
I kinda know what you mean!

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:59.840
Finish your old stuff before you buy new ones.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:00.760
Well...

00:19:00.760 --> 00:19:03.510
It's reassuring if I buy it first.

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:06.140
Or I end up feeling unsatisfied otherwise.

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:06.760
Right?

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.010
Don't look at me.

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:14.980
Good lucky!

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:15.900
Okay!

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:18.650
Let's have a blast today!

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:23.320
We're already on the seventeenth episode of Lucky Channel.

00:19:23.320 --> 00:19:24.030
Okay!

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:25.110
Your navigator...

00:19:25.110 --> 00:19:27.280
Red roses have thorns!

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.330
The platypus of the idol world!

00:19:29.330 --> 00:19:31.910
Akira Kogami!

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:32.290
And...

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:32.790
Hello!

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:35.670
...we've invited a really big guest today!

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:39.420
How long are you going to make me wait?!

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:41.210
Crap.

00:19:41.210 --> 00:19:42.800
He really did come back.
Sorry, sorry.

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:43.880
Here he is...

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:46.470
Um...

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:47.930
Today's guest...

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:48.930
...is the Anime Manager:

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:50.600
Meito Anizawa-san.

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:51.430
Okay!

00:19:51.430 --> 00:19:53.560
This program is too weak!

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:55.100
But...

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:56.020
Um...

00:19:56.020 --> 00:20:00.400
Lucky Star is a slow and relaxed anime...

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:03.740
...about completely ordinary high school students.

00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:04.780
Which is why...

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:07.200
...Lucky Channel should be considered...

00:20:07.200 --> 00:20:10.160
...slow rather than...

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:11.620
That won't work!

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:12.430
Where'd he go?!

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:17.210
Fast!

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.460
Listen.

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:22.430
Do you know what the three factors
for determining an anime's success are?

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:23.880
The three factors?

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:24.630
Um...

00:20:24.630 --> 00:20:26.720
Voice actors, animation, and script?

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:28.680
Wrong!

00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:32.100
This back of mine is burning red!

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:33.100
The answer is...

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:34.060
The answer is?

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.480
The staff and cast's love for the show!

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:38.350
And time!

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:40.270
And production cost!

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:43.900
Well, those factors are all out of our control...

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:47.530
Understand?

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:49.160
It doesn't matter how good the original work was!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.370
There's no point if the script is bad!

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:53.120
It doesn't matter how hard the voice actors work!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:56.290
It won't work out if the characters aren't in colour!

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:57.750
Just look at Shiraishi.

00:20:57.870 --> 00:20:58.710
N-Now I'm white(shiroi)!

00:20:59.040 --> 00:21:02.420
Each respective part requires its resources!

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:04.300
You have to put your all into the work!

00:21:04.300 --> 00:21:06.420
Love and passion are what...

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:11.220
...truly create a beautiful piece of work!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.720
Is that how it works?

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:15.100
You.

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:16.680
You're currently Akira Kogami-san, correct?

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:18.140
Currently?

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:20.850
I've always been Akira.

00:21:21.060 --> 00:21:22.310
When you were Rou**n!

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:23.150
Gao**nger!

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:23.730
**tato!

00:21:23.730 --> 00:21:24.770
Mai**i!

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:26.900
Didn't you have love?!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:28.530
What are you talking about?

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:31.570
If you still have regrets...

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:32.240
Nope. None.

00:21:32.240 --> 00:21:34.990
...you should burn yourself out as Akira Kogami!

00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:36.290
Like I was saying...

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:36.950
Okay!

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:39.620
I will burn myself out as Minoru Shiraishi!

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:42.000
Well said, Shiraishi!

00:21:42.330 --> 00:21:44.590
Okay, first of all.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:45.170
How to work a live event!

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:45.880
Over?

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:46.130
How to work a live event!

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:47.590
You MC'd an event recently, right?

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:48.880
Bye-bee...

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:49.470
You MC'd an event recently, right?

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.010
You were watching?

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:51.430
Of course! It's my job!

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:52.550
Good work, everyone!

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:53.430
It was a huge job.

00:21:53.430 --> 00:21:53.470
I'm leaving now..

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:54.970
My nerves were a wreck the whole time

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:55.390
I'm leaving now...

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:55.720
You still have a lot to learn!

00:21:55.720 --> 00:21:56.600
Shiraishi can handle the rest.

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:57.680
First, your ad libs are weak!

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:57.890
Yes!

00:21:57.890 --> 00:21:58.980
You shouldn't be losing to Sugita—

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:01.030
Ma'am!

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:02.300
Are you unsatisfied with your husband?

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:03.670
Hello. Minoru Shiraishi here.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.170
Now, please listen to me!

00:22:24.790 --> 00:22:25.420
FeeLING crummy!

00:22:25.420 --> 00:22:25.990
SomethING's coming!

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:26.690
I LOVE you so!

00:22:26.690 --> 00:22:26.890
Oops!

00:22:26.890 --> 00:22:28.060
I screwed one upsie-up!

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:28.630
A nail biter!

00:22:28.630 --> 00:22:29.290
A steel beater!

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:31.060
Cut that out already!

00:22:31.060 --> 00:22:32.930
Is that new blushing flower...

00:22:32.930 --> 00:22:34.500
...considered a normal girl or what?

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:35.070
Wowzers!

00:22:35.630 --> 00:22:35.970
Take it!

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:36.400
Firm noodles!

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:36.770
Fill 'er up again!

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:37.970
DA-DA-DA!

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:44.740
BON-BON

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:45.780
Cheerleaders!

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:50.510
How about it?

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:51.180
Yeah!

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:52.280
Leavin' an impression.

00:22:57.020 --> 00:22:58.320
Take it!

00:22:58.320 --> 00:23:02.790
I'll still be laughing in the end!

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:06.730
'Cause it's a sailor uniform.

00:23:06.730 --> 00:23:08.300
← Q.E.D.!

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:10.720
It's only Sunday and I'm already blue.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:11.770
※Fast forwarded for your convenience.

00:23:11.770 --> 00:23:12.740
What to do?

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:14.470
I'd rather wear my summer clothes

00:23:14.470 --> 00:23:15.740
← So cute!

00:23:16.010 --> 00:23:16.670
3 pics incoming!

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:17.240
That's a toughie to pick!

00:23:17.240 --> 00:23:17.410
Ooh ☆

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:17.710
Just work it!

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:18.180
To the limit!

00:23:18.180 --> 00:23:19.680
MY DARLIN' DARLIN! PLEASE!!

00:23:20.940 --> 00:23:21.320
Well, next time...

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:22.860
Too boring, Shiraishi!

00:23:22.860 --> 00:23:24.610
Stop following protocol!

00:23:24.610 --> 00:23:25.400
Heil Braiking!

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:26.020
Manager!

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:26.610
Okay!

00:23:26.610 --> 00:23:27.860
Now listen to me!

00:23:27.860 --> 00:23:29.490
Lessons on how to become a big-time voice actor!

00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:30.330
Number one!

00:23:30.330 --> 00:23:31.870
Lesson number one!

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:33.700
If you can't beat them, join them.

00:23:33.700 --> 00:23:34.960
That's sad!

00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:35.500
Next time:

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:36.750
To Each Her Own!

00:23:36.750 --> 00:23:38.290
That's it for Anizawa. Goodbye.

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:39.500
Finger!
